2 CONT Giovanni Michiel was raised—like his cousin Giovanni Battista Zeno, son of Niccolò and '''Elisabetta Barbo, who, like M.'s mother, was the sister of the next pontiff [i.e. Pope Paul II]'''—in Rome at the home of his cardinal uncle
2 CONC  (therefore, the report of M. and Zeno having received a joint degree from Padua is unreliable ). The elevation of Pietro Barbo to the papal throne with the name Paul II on August 30, 1464, favored him.
