1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Evidence needed to support Philippe Mius d'Entremont (https://www.geni.com/people/Baron-Philippe-Mius/6000000002627510001) as son of https://www.geni.com/people/Claude-Antoine-Dalbon/6000000003151356491 and his wife https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/people/Beatrice-d-Entremont/6000000211011214821?through=6000000003151356491
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacqueline_de_Montbel_d%27Entremont
2 CONT Enfant: '''Beatrix de Coligny, Comtesse d'Entremont ''' (d) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Succession
2 CONT
2 CONT *Béatrice de Coligny, (Daughter of Jacqueline de Montbel d'Entremont), Countess of Montbel d'Entremont, (1572-…), married the November 30, 1600 Claude-Antoine Bon, Lord Baron of Meuillon. (…-1618), to whom the fiefs and the name o
2 CONC f Montbel passed.
2 CONT **François Bon, known as d'Albon, Count of Montbel and d'Entremont, married Madeleine du Tillet. (François Virginie Bon, comte d'Entremont et de Montbel (1601 - 1671).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Coligny-36
2 CONT Daughter of Gaspard (Coligny) de Coligny 
2 CONT and Jacqueline (Montbel) de Montbel d'Entremont
2 CONT [ [https://www.geni.com/people/Philippe-Mius/6000000002627510001 children unknown] ]
2 CONT
2 CONT   Biography.. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle est peut-être la mère de [https://www.geni.com/people/Philippe-Mius/6000000002627510001 Philippe Mius], baron de Pobomcoup.
2 CONT 1. Internet - e-mail de "Serrod" deTreville (vert@compuzone.net)
2 CONT 2. Internet - e-mail de Michel Azit (azitca@yahoo.ca) du 12 mars 2003
2 CONT Source: Généalogie Québec - http://www.genealogiequebec.info/frames.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Disputed son
2 CONT
2 CONT "De Coligny, De Laval, Musse, De Meullon, d'Entremont"
2 CONT Discussion archived at < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/xDeiQixytmQ/m/hDoLfCSwNjkJ groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval] >
2 CONT Jan 16, 1999, 1:00:00 AM message from William Addams Reitwiesner
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/xDeiQixytmQ/m/hDoLfCSwNjkJ
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I'm afraid the verification [of the ancestry of Philippe Mius d'Entremont] is going to be negative. There's a genealogy of the Colignys in *Europaeische Stammtafeln*, ed. Schwennicke, Band XIV [1991], Taf. 60-64. Gaspard II, Admir
2 CONC al of France, appears on Tafel 61. He married twice, his first wife (marriage contract dated at Fontainebleau on 15 October 1547) was Charlotte de Laval (d. 1568), by whom he had eight children. His second wife (married at La Roch
2 CONC elle 25 March 1571) was Jacqueline de Montbel (born at Paris in 1541, imprisoned in 1573 and died, still in captivity, at the Castello d'Ivrea in December 1599). Jacqueline was the widow of Claude de Batarnay, Count du Bouchage.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Gaspard was killed in the St Bartholomew's night massacre (24 August 1572), Jacqueline gave birth to their only child, Beatrix de Coligny, at Saint-Andre-de Briord on 21 December 1572. Beatrix married at Turin on 30 November
2 CONC  1600 (contract dated 17 July 1600) Claude Antoine d'Albon, Baron de Mevouillon et de Montauban, who died 26 February 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude Antoine, son-in-law of the Admiral of France, wasn't named "Mius DE MEULLON". What's your source that says he was?
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==Older genealogy
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliothèque et Archives Canada < [https://epe.lac-bac.gc.ca/100/205/301/ic/cdc/argyle/html/fgenealogie4.htm link] >. "Lettre à Eugene à Hilaire d'Entremont"  (Google translation from French)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT NB Copy of a letter that was found at Eugene's to Hilaire d'Entremont very recently. It does not bear a signature. Father Clarence d'Entremont believes that it was written by his uncle Léander d'Entremont.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is with great pleasure that I will tell you that I have succeeded, in my research on our family, in finding the complete genealogy of d'Entremont, a fact which the greatest historians of France and Canada have never been able t
2 CONC o make progress on. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix, Countess of Montbel and d'Entremont, Marquise of Montellier and Saint-André-de-Briord, Lady-in-waiting to Catherine, Infanta of Spain, Duchess of Savoy, married, on November 30, 1600, Claude Antoine Bon, Baron de Meuillon
2 CONC , Governor of Marseille. From this marriage came several children, namely:
2 CONT
2 CONT # François Virginie , [known as Philippe Mius,] Count of Entremont and Montbel, Marquis of Montellier, Lord of Chatillon, heir to his mother's property, born in 1603; he married Madeleine Elie, daughter of Elie du Tillet, Lord of 
2 CONC Nogeage and Françoise de Faucon. Philippe traveled to America in 1651. '''comment: he was not known as Philippe Mius and he did not travel to America.'''
2 CONT # N............ of Meuillon, known as the Abbot of Entremont.
2 CONT # Baron de Nottage.
2 CONT # And n....... of Meuillon, Carmelite nun in Chaumont, founder of this convent. (The males of this house were obliged to bear the arms of Montbel and d'Entremont).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # SOURCE: http://www.lagenealogy.net/pages/mius.aspx (dead link)
2 CONT # https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacqueline_de_Montbel_d%27Entremont "December 21, 1572, Jacqueline gives birth to a little girl who is named Beatrice, in homage to her grandmother. One of the conditions for the return of Madame l'
2 CONC amirale de Coligny to Savoy was not only her conversion to Catholicism, but also the Catholic baptism of her child. ... 
2 CONT # Genealogical and heraldic history of the peers of France: from ..., Volume 12.  By Jean Baptiste Pierre Jullien de Courcelles.  Page 54.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=mksWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA54&lpg=PA54&dq=Sieur+Claude+Antoine
2 CONC +d%27Albon&source=bl&ots=3CNAEqFxWF&sig=lRdK_t6HCTXyDjOMZ9p6Xj-CbHk&hl=en&ei=v9HoSfTPJ4KltgfVr-DTBQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result#v=onepage&q=Sieur%20Claude%20Antoine%20d'Albon&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT # https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/236447075/b%C3%A9atrice_de_coligny
