1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gaspard, known as the Marshal of Châtillon, was a French soldier. He served in the Italian Wars from 1495 to 1515, and was created Marshal of France in 1516.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife, Louise de Montmorency, sister of the future constable, he had three sons: Odet, Cardinal de Châtillon; Gaspard, the Admiral; and François, Seigneur d'Andelot. All three played an important part in the first period of 
2 CONC the Wars of Religion.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaspard_I_de_Coligny
