3 CITY Salzburg
3 CTRY Erzherzogtum Österreich, H.R.R
1 OCCU
1 TITL Graf
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00090689&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Jan Josef was born in Unter-Cerau, Carinthia, on 9 April 1652, the son of Graf Johann Friedrich von Küenburg zu Ungersbach and Johanna de Guzmán de Silva. On 10 September 1679 he married Gräfin Maria Claudia zu Sulz, dau
2 CONC ghter of Graf Johann Ludwig II von Sulz, Landgraf im Klettgau, and Gräfin Maria Elisabeth von Königsegg-Aulendorf. She died in 1681 without progeny, and on 6 March 1682 he married Gräfin Josepha von Harrach zu Rohrau, the eldest d
2 CONC aughter of Graf Ferdinand Bonaventura I von Harrach and Johanna Theresia von Lamberg. They had at least nine children, of whom a son and two daughters would have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan Josef inherited the estate and castle of Mladá Vozice (Jungwoschitz) in Southern Bohemia as an entailed estate from his elder brother Franz Ferdinand (1651-1731), archbishop of Prague. Franz Ferdinand had inherited it in 1678,
2 CONC  and developed in the castle a significant baroque library, to which he added Italian and French literature gathered in his diplomatic missions to southern Europe. Another contributor to the library was his relative, the archbisho
2 CONC p of Salzburg Maximilian Gandolph von Küenburg (1622-1687). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan Josef died in Salzburg on 7 March 1726.
