1 OCCU duc de Châtillon,  duc de Coligny, marquis d'Andelot, seigneur de Châtillon-sur-Loing, Pair et maréchal de France (1622).
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaspard_III_de_Coligny
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaspard III de Coligny, Maréchal de Châtillon, of the House of Coligny ( 26 July 1584, Montpellier-4 January 1646, Châtillon), comte de Coligny and seigneur de Châtillon-sur-Loing, then duc de Coligny, marquis d'Andelot, Peer of F
2 CONC rance, Marshal of France (1622), was a French Protestant general.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of François de Coligny (1557–1591) and his wife Marguerite d'Ailly, and the grandson of admiral Gaspard de Coligny.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Thirty Years' War, he won the Battle of Les Avins against a Spanish army under Thomas Francis, Prince of Carignan. On 6 July 1641, Gaspard de Coligny commanded the army of Louis XIII at the Battle of La Marfée, where he
2 CONC  was defeated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 August 1615 he married Anne de Polignac (1598–1651), and they had 4 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice (16 October 1618 at Châtillon-sur-Loing-23 May 1644 at Vincennes), Comte de Coligny, died in a duel with the duc de Guise)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaspard IV de Coligny (9 June 1620 at Châtillon-sur-Loing-9 February 1649 Château de Vincennes), duc de Châtillon then duc de Coligny 1648, marshal of France (1649). In 1645 married Élisabeth Angélique de Montmorency-Bouteville (1
2 CONC 627–1695)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henriette de Coligny (1618–1673), in 1643 married Thomas Hamilton, Earl of Haddington , then in 1653 married Gaspard de Champagne, comte de la Suze (marriage annulled).
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne, (4 September 1624 at Châtillon-sur-Loing-13 January 1680 at Riquewir), in 1648 married George II, duke of Wurtemberg-Montbéliard (1626–1699)
