1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Ferry II de Mailly, Seigneur de Conty1
2 CONT *'''M, #152383, b. circa 1478, d. 1512
2 CONT *Father	Adrien de Mailly1 b. c 1438, d. 4 Sep 1518
2 CONT *Mother	Jeanne de Berghes1
2 CONT *'''     Ferry II de Mailly, Seigneur de Conty was born circa 1478 at of Mailly-Maillet, Somme, Picardie, France.1 He married Louise de Montmorency''', daughter of William de Montmorency, Baron de Montmorency, d'Ecouen, Chantilly,
2 CONC  & Damville and Anne Pot, '''circa 1504.1 Ferry II de Mailly, Seigneur de Conty died in 1512 at Milan, Lombardy, Italy.1
2 CONT *'''Family     Louise de Montmorency b. c 1485, d. 22 Jun 1541
2 CONT *Child	
2 CONT **Madeleine de Mailly+1 b. c 1507, d. c 1570
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S59] GeneaNet, Gérard DuPond de la Marteloye de Cercamp site.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p5075.htm#i152383 ______________
2 CONT *'''Louise de Montmorency''' (1496–1547) was a French noblewoman from the ancient House of Montmorency.
2 CONT *She was the younger sister of Anne de Montmorency, Constable of France, and the mother of Gaspard de Coligny, Admiral of France.
2 CONT *'''Louise married her first husband, Ferri de Mailly, in 1511.[1] This marriage produced a daughter''', Madeleine de Mailly. '''Ferry died in 1513, and Louise remarried''' in 1514 to Gaspard I de Coligny. From her second marriage
2 CONC  she had three sons, all of whom played important roles in the first period of the French Wars of Religion: Odet, Cardinal de Châtillon; Gaspard, the Admiral; and François, Seigneur d'Andelot.
2 CONT *She had considerable patronage power independently of her husband,[2][3] and had an important role in spreading the influence of Calvinism in France in the 16th Century.[4]
