1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henriette_de_Coligny_de_La_Suze
2 CONT
2 CONT Henriette de Coligny de La Suze (1618 – March 10, 1673) was a French writer.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Gaspard III de Coligny and Anne de Polignac. She was married twice: first, in 1643, to Thomas Hamilton, 3rd Earl of Haddington, who died in February 1645, and then, in 1647, to Gaspard de Champagne, comte d
2 CONC e la Suze. Originally a Protestant, she converted to Catholicism in 1653. Her second marriage was annulled in 1661 on the grounds of impotence.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1666, she published a collection of 21 of her poems as Poésies de Madame la Comtesse de La Suze but she also contributed verse and prose to many other collected works. Ninety-five of her poems appear in "L'amour raisonnable", p
2 CONC art of Recueil de pièces galantes en prose et en vers; each poem is preceded by a preamble in prose.
2 CONT
2 CONT De La Suze was admired by the writers Madeleine de Scudéry and Paul Pellisson.
