1 FAMS @F6000000001111336715@
1 RFN geni:6000000008854222920
1 SUBM @S6000000000408818051@
1 NOTE Seigneur Pierre D'Mailly was a French Huguenot. Seigneur Pierre D'Mailly changed his name to Mabille after fleeing from France to Holland during the St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre in 1572. August 24, 1572, was the date of the infa
2 CONC mous St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre in France. On that day, began one of the most horrifying holocausts in history.
2 CONT
2 CONT #
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur Pierre d'Mailly, a French Huguenot, was driven out of France due to his unpopular religious beliefs, escaping to Holland, where he changed his name to Mabille. 
