2 CONT Gebeurtenisse:
2 CONT
2 CONT a.	Jean II de Montmorency remains constantly loyal to King Charles VII in its struggles against the English.
2 CONT
2 CONT b.	In retaliation, the King of England confiscated his lands including that of Montmorency, and gives them to one of his supporters, Jean of Luxembourg bastard de St Pol.  Charles VII became victorious.
2 CONT
2 CONT c.	Jean II De Montmorency(1401-1477) was made Chamberlain of France in 1425 by King Charles VII (1403 to 1422 -1461) and confirmed in office by King Louis XI (1423-1461 -1483). Faithful to the king, he had joined Joan of Arc and i
2 CONC n the War of the League of Public Good (1465), he sided with the king against the nobles.  d.	Around 1463 his son come to blows for a heritage history; the eldest is injured. Jean Louis and take refuge in their strongholds of Flan
2 CONC ders. Jean 11 de Montmorency disinherited them. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e.	Epitaph of John II of Montmorency:-
2 CONT
2 CONT Here lies noble and powerful lord, lord lord Jehan de Montmorency, first Baron of France, formerly Lord said Montmorency and Damville, Ecouen, Vitry, Conflans and Tour-au-Begue, counselor and chamberlain of the King our Lord, who 
2 CONC passed away on 6 July in the year 1477. Pray that forgiveness makes him to eternity. Amen-Ingestuur Ds. MG Müller
2 CONT
