1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Enr%C3%ADquez_de_Acevedo
2 CONT
2 CONT http://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=es&u=http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Enr%25C3%25ADquez_de_Acevedo&ei=tUDPT4PhGMON6QG2oIywDA&sa=X&oi=translate&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CE8Q7gEwAA&prev=/search%3Fq%3DPedro%2BEnr%25C3
2 CONC %25ADquez%2Bde%2BAcevedo,%2Bconde%2Bde%2BFuentes%26hl%3Den%26biw%3D1600%26bih%3D805%26prmd%3Dimvnsbo
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro Enriquez de Acevedo ( Zamora , September 18th of 1525 - Milan , July 22 of 1610 ), Count of Fuentes , the Spanish political and military. Son of Don Diego Enriquez de Guzman, 3rd Count Alba de Liste (List) and Dona Catalina 
2 CONC de Toledo and Pimentel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his marriage in 1585 to Dona Juana de Acevedo y Fonseca, first Countess of Fuentes , he adopted his name and title, the first Earl of sources . 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1585 he was appointed captain general of the cavalry of Milan , under the orders of the governor of Milan Sancho de Guevara and Padilla. In 1589 be appointed captain-general of Portugal , defended Lisbon attack by Antonio I of 
2 CONC Portugal , who was assisted by the English John Norreys and Francis Drake , privateers sent by Elizabeth I of England . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Since in 1595 the head of the thirds of Flanders , took Dourlens and Cambrai ( 1595 ), in the course of the war against France . For her merits, Philip II appointed him in 1598 , captain-general of Spain , Minister of State and Wa
2 CONC r and grandee of Spain . 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1600 he was appointed governor of Milan , where he became one of the great politicians peripheral monarchy Philip III who defended the prestige of Spain outside their borders against the pacifist policy of the Duke of Lerma . H
2 CONC is performance was directed to securing for the Spanish troops in transit from Italy to Germany and Flanders , through the Valtellina , where they built the famous fort that bears his name. 
