2 CONT Philibert II, Duke of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert II (10 April 1480 – 10 September 1504), surnamed the Handsome or the Good was the Duke of Savoy from 1497 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Pont-d'Ain, he was the son of Philip (Filippo) the Landless, who until 1496 was a younger son of the ducal family of Savoy, and his first wife Marguerite of Bourbon. In 1496, Philibert's father surprisingly succeeded as Du
2 CONC ke, when his underaged great-grandnephew Duke Charles II of Savoy died, being the male heir of the line of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT The same year, the 16-year-old Philibert married the 9-year-old Yolande Louise of Savoy, his cousin and the only sister of the deceased young duke. She was daughter of Duke Charles I of Savoy, the Warrior, and Blanche of Montferra
2 CONC t, as well as granddaughter of Philibert's late uncle, Duke Amedeo IX of Savoy. She was the heir-general of her brother, father, grandfather, and also grandmother Yolande of France, the eldest surviving daughter of king Charles VI
2 CONC I of France. Her birth-right, after the death of her brother, was the succession of the kingdoms of Cyprus and Jerusalem, although Philibert's father took those titles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Next year, Philibert's father died and he succeeded as Duke of Savoy. The young couple then at last advanced their claims, and took the titles Queen and King of Cyprus, Jerusalem and Armenia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1499, the 12-year-old first wife of Philibert died, childless. Her heir was her first cousin, Princess Charlotte of Naples, later Countess of Laval. Philibert continued to use the titles of Cyprus etc, despite the death of his 
2 CONC first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT His next marriage tied him into the web of alliances around the Imperial Habsburgs, who ruled The Netherlands, Alsace and Franche-Comté, Tirol, Austria, etc. He married the only daughter of Emperor Maximilian I and his late wife M
2 CONC ary of Burgundy, heiress of Flanders, Palatine Burgundy, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT During Philibert's reign, his first cousin Charles VIII of France died, and the next king, Louis XII of France, invaded Italy, where he conquered most of the Kingdom of Naples. He also conquered Milan, which neighboured Savoy to t
2 CONC he east, putting the Savoyards between French possessions.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, he died childless, and relatively young, at 24. He was succeeded by his young half-brother Charles III in 1504.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert married:
2 CONT
2 CONT Yolande Louise (1487-1499), daughter of his first cousin, Carlo I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Austria (1480-1530) who was Governor of the Seventeen Provinces of the Netherlands (1507-1515, 1519-1530) and a daughter of Maximilian I and Mary of Burgundy and had no children from this marriage.
